==European competitions==

As runners-up in the 2007 Finnish Cup to Tampere United, who had also won the league title, FC Honka qualified for the [[2008–09 UEFA Cup]], beating the [[Iceland]]ic club [[Íþróttabandalag Akraness|ÍA]] 4–2 in the 1st qualifying round and the [[Norway|Norwegian]] club [[Viking FK|Viking]] in the 2nd. In the first round of actual competition, they were drawn against [[Racing de Santander|Racing Santander]] and lost 0–2 on aggregate.

Next year, Honka qualified for the new [[2009–10 UEFA Europa League|UEFA Europa League]], starting from the second qualifying round. The club beat Welsh side [[Bangor City F.C.]] 3–0 on aggregate but lost 1–3 to [[FK Karabakh]] from Azerbaijan in the third qualifying round.

For the [[2010–11 UEFA Europa League|2010–11 season]], FC Honka was again drawn against Bangor City in the second round but lost 3–2 on aggregate.

During the winter of 2009, Honka won the annual [[La Manga Cup]], beating [[FC Nordsjælland]] in the final.

